  "text": "ordinarium.praefatio-sacratissimi-cordis-iesu",
  "about": "The Preface of the Most Sacred Heart of Jesus. It presents Christ's pierced Heart as the shrine of divine bounty, the source of mercy and grace, and a refuge of salvation.",
  "segments": {
    "s01": { "narrative": "Then the priest separates his hands and holds them apart until the end of the Preface. When it is finished, he joins them again and, bowing, says: Sanctus." },
    "s02": { "translation": "It is truly meet and just, right and profitable for salvation, that we should at all times and in all places give thanks unto Thee:" },
    "s03": { "translation": "O Lord, holy Father, almighty and eternal God:" },
    "s04": { "translation": "Who didst will that Thine only-begotten Son, hanging upon the Cross, should be pierced by a soldier's lance, that His opened Heart, the shrine of divine bounty, might pour forth upon us streams of mercy and grace; and that the Heart which never ceased to burn with love for us might be a rest for the devout and might lie open to the penitent as a refuge of salvation." },
    "s05": { "translation": "And therefore with Angels and Archangels, with Thrones and Dominations, and with all the host of the heavenly army, we sing the hymn of Thy glory, saying without end:" }
  },
